        1811,
        1111
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Hours is a program that is catching on in all the business districts of Manhattan. The 1972 goal of the Staggered Work Hours Program in lower Manhattan is enlarged participation — a total of 120,000 people on new working hours in the business and governmental community. After the success in lower Manhattan, a similar project has started in Midtown Manhattan under the auspices of the Midtown Task Force on Staggered Work Hours. As more and more employers and employees learn of the benefits of Staggered Work Hours, the results in greater personal comfort, better use of our transportation systems, and improved business will become increasingly evident.",
